{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":70943,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"33613058-5319-56fc-98be-b08864aade72","total_cost_usd":0.296398,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12650,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6408,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12650,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6408,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12650},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9598,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.009688,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6408,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":12650,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.28671,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:stage1-recovery-claude-04\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires a rate for the entire scheduled survey network (the complete domain of 96 scheduled stations).\",\"observed_value\":\"complete-domain target\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result uses the complete scheduled-station denominator (96), not the retained subset (72); 18/96 = 0.1875 matches the complete-domain exposure.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/96 = 0.1875\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow code that emits the selected result divides observed occurrences by SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96), confirming the report line is not a stale or inconsistent artifact.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96 used as denominator\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":6,\"quoted_text\":\"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF\"}]},{\"description\":\"Row-level data support the reported counts: 96 data rows all with scheduled=yes, 24 rows marked omitted with occurrence_flag NA, and 18 retained rows with occurrence_flag 1 (six per North/Central/South, none in Outer).\",\"observed_value\":\"96 scheduled rows; 24 omitted; 18 occurrence flags of 1\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-001,North,yes,retained,none,1\\nCS-002,North,yes,retained,none,0\\nCS-003,North,yes,retained,none,0\\nCS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":94,\"end_line\":97,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-093,Outer,yes,retained,none,0\\nCS-094,Outer,yes,retained,none,0\\nCS-095,Outer,yes,retained,none,0\\nCS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Falsification probe: the numerator is drawn only from retained stations, which could in principle indicate a hidden retained-subset framing; however the report explicitly assigns the 24 unobserved stations zero occurrences within the 96-station denominator and labels the result a lower bound, so the reported rate is a complete-domain rate rather than a retained-subset rate.\",\"observed_value\":\"numerator restricted to retained stations but denominator complete, disclosed as lower bound\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":11,\"quoted_text\":\"Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":19,\"quoted_text\":\"The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the no-issue verdict by searching for any selected or headline rate whose denominator equals the retained subset (72). I checked the selected-result line, the exposure-denominator line, the workflow string that builds the selected result, and the limitations section: the denominator constant used is SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96, the arithmetic 18/96 = 0.1875 is consistent with the complete-domain denominator, and results/report.md L0019 explicitly states no screened-subset rate is reported. I also checked whether the 72-station count appears anywhere as an exposure base and found it only as a descriptive count on results/report.md L0009. No retained-subset denominator underlies the reported claim, so the in-scope mismatch could not be demonstrated.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:35069763f06891dba5a3\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"bounded_statement\":\"The selected result claims an occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network (96 scheduled stations) but computes it as 18/72 using only the screen-retained subset as the exposure denominator, excluding the 24 screened-out scheduled stations from the denominator; the complete-domain denominator entailed by the stated task and the report's own target population is 96, so the reported 0.25 overstates the complete-network rate relative to the 18/96 = 0.1875 complete-domain computation.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow hard-codes the retained-subset count SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 as the exposure denominator in the selected-result line while labelling that quantity a rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', so the 24 screen-omitted but scheduled stations are dropped from the exposure base rather than retained with zero observed occurrences.\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network, i.e. the complete domain of scheduled stations.\",\"observed_value\":\"complete-domain target\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's own stated target population is all 96 scheduled stations, not the screened subset.\",\"observed_value\":\"target population = 96 scheduled stations\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result asserts a rate for the entire scheduled survey network while dividing by the 72 retained stations, i.e. a retained-subset exposure denominator carrying a complete-domain claim.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/72 = 0.25 labelled as entire-network rate\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations).\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow code builds the selected line using SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) as the divisor while the scheduled count 96 exists as a separate constant, confirming the denominator choice is in the code and not a transcription slip.\",\"observed_value\":\"SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 used as divisor\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96\\nSCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72\\nOMITTED_STATIONS = 24\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF\"}]},{\"description\":\"Row-level data show the 24 excluded stations are scheduled units (scheduled=yes) that were merely screened out, so they belong to the complete scheduled domain the claim covers.\",\"observed_value\":\"omitted rows carry scheduled=yes\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":97,\"end_line\":97,\"quoted_text\":\"CS-096,Outer,yes,omitted,screen_fail_data_gap,NA\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Falsification probe: the report transparently discloses the retained/omitted counts and names the 72-station denominator, which might be read as an explicitly conditional target; however the disclosure is only descriptive accounting and the selected claim and stated target population remain the entire 96-station scheduled network, and the report states no method deviation was approved, so transparency does not convert the claim into a subset-conditional one.\",\"observed_value\":\"denominator disclosed but claim scope unchanged; no approved deviation\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":9,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"Stations passing the signal screen: 72\\nStations omitted by the signal screen: 24\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I tried to falsify the issue by looking for any statement that makes the target explicitly conditional on passing the signal screen, which would place the case outside scope. task.md L0001 asks for a rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network'; results/report.md L0004 states the target population as 'all 96 scheduled coastal stations'; and the selected-result line itself is labelled 'for the entire scheduled survey network'. No conditional-on-screen framing exists anywhere. I next tried to falsify the arithmetic premise by checking whether the excluded 24 rows might be out-of-domain (unscheduled) units; every omitted row in inputs/data.csv carries scheduled=yes, so they are inside the claimed domain. Finally I checked whether a complete-domain rate was reported elsewhere in the report and found none, and results/report.md L0018 confirms no approved deviation licenses the subset denominator. The mismatch survives all three attempts.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"},{\"case_id\":\"case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The stated scientific question is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen, so the retained (signal-eligible) subset is the intended domain.\",\"observed_value\":\"explicitly conditional target\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"task.md\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":1,\"quoted_text\":\"Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report declares the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations and scopes the selected result explicitly to signal-eligible stations, so denominator and claim scope match.\",\"observed_value\":\"target = 72 eligible; claim scoped 'Among signal-eligible stations'\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":8,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow code labels the selected result with the conditional scope and divides by SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS, consistent with the conditional target.\",\"observed_value\":\"18/72 with 'Among signal-eligible stations' label\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":18,\"end_line\":18,\"quoted_text\":\"RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF\"}]},{\"description\":\"Input accounting distinguishes the 24 stations outside the eligible set as not assessed for occurrence, matching the report's disposition of those units.\",\"observed_value\":\"24 outside_signal_eligible, not_assessed\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/data.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":4,\"quoted_text\":\"signal_eligible_occurrence,18,observed\\nsignal_eligible_no_occurrence,54,not_observed\\noutside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Falsification probe: the report also states the full scheduled network of 96 stations, which could suggest a complete-domain claim; but that line is descriptive context only, the 24 non-eligible stations are separately accounted for as not assessed, and no rate is asserted over the 96-station domain, so the complete-domain figure is not used as or presented as the selected claim.\",\"observed_value\":\"96-station network stated as context, no 96-denominator rate claimed\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":3,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"Scheduled network: 96 stations.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"Planned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the no-issue verdict by testing whether the reported claim actually requires the complete 96-station domain despite the subset denominator. I examined task.md L0001, which states the scientific question is 'conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen'; results/report.md L0004, which names the target population as the 72 signal-eligible stations; and the selected-result line, which is explicitly prefixed 'Among signal-eligible stations'. I then checked whether any sentence generalises the 25% figure to the scheduled network and found none — the only complete-domain mention (L0003) is bare context, and L0005 explicitly records the 24 excluded stations as not assessed. Because the target is explicitly conditional on the retained subset, the in-scope mismatch is excluded by definition.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":15058,"ttft_stream_ms":2101,"time_to_request_ms":85,"type":"result","duration_ms":70685,"uuid":"2df83790-425f-4994-90b8-5304b2cffdf8"}
